From 50416ff3ea1fa18ce6fe3fec62aace5575d5e0d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:24:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] VideoOutput: draw the views of a 10, 12 and 16 bit depth
 video on the GPU at the source's depth, import the decoder's frames, tell the
 GPU's memory

Deep colour on the GPU path. P010, P016, YUV420P10, YUV422P16 and YUV444P16 frames (every high bit depth format the FFmpeg backend hands
Qt here) go to the passes as the words they are: R16 and RG16 textures (GL_EXT_texture_norm16 on OpenGL ES, said when it is missing), the
conversion shader reads the code of each format (P010 and the 16 bit formats hold it in the high bits, YUV420P10 in the low bits; limited
and full range, BT.601, BT.709, BT.2020), the picture and the views are RGBA16, the depth samples are R16UI integers read through the 1024 or
65536 entry table of the C code, the colour textures of the passes are half float up to 10 bits and float above, and the views leave in the
source's pixel format and depth (an encode pass writes the Y and CbCr planes at the source's depth, the chroma of a subsampled format from
the mean of the block of pixels it covers): the full side by side frame is never cut to 8 bits. The C code is used for deep content only
when the person asks for the processor, and the log says so.

Hardware frames without the read back. A frame the decoder keeps on a GPU (VA-API) is mapped into the drawing context by the decoder's
own texture converter (QHwVideoBuffer::mapTextures through a QRhi that shares the drawing context) and the passes read its planes where
they are: no copy to system memory. A converter that refuses the frame (a DMA-BUF the drawing GPU cannot import), a turned frame, or the
copy asked for (QT_MM_DEPTH_COPY_FRAMES, Options::importFrames) copies it, counted (Renderer::hardwareReadBacks()) and said in the log of
qt.multimedia.video.depth with the reason.

GPU memory. VideoOutput::stereoDepthGpuMemory tells what the drawing GPU has free and the size and depth of the views, for the controls to
say beside a way that would not fit; the ways are timed and judged at the depth of the content.

Tests: tst_qquickvideostereo depthOnTheGpuKeepsTheDepth (a ramp whose low bits an 8 bit truncation loses, with its control),
depthImportsHardwareFrames (mapTextures through a fake hardware buffer: zero read backs, the same views; the copy asked for and a refusing
converter read back and say so), depthDeepCases (the 10 and 16 bit versions of the depth cases against the C code, DEEP_CASES).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
